/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5cae1fd22b1e18b4461c39cf1037217cd3796498a0960b0386be8472969e06a" "basis" 2612 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda >0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions ${y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(\\pi )=0$ yields $A=0.$ Thus, we have a nontrivial solution, so $\\lambda =0$ is a parameter corresponding to the eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda >0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+25\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 5\\text{i}\\sqrt{\\lambda }.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x\\sqrt{\\lambda }),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x\\sqrt{\\lambda })\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-5A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+5B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-5A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+5B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $B=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-5A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi \\sqrt{\\lambda })=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n5\\pi \\sqrt{\\lambda }=n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}}{25}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}}),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5cae1fd22b1e18b4461c39cf1037217cd3796498a0960b0386be8472969e06a" "basis" 2612 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c72764fbd932c6506ae2af080dac9b2ff7abceca44e7e85139d6000ba16c77e" "basis" 2612 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338921" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5cae1fd22b1e18b4461c39cf1037217cd3796498a0960b0386be8472969e06a" "basis" 2612 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071917/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338921" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{10}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14